uration information from your targeted environment through an internal service-to-service authorization. The policy allows for Security and Compliance Center to read the configuration but the service is unable to change it in any way. Collected data includes the properties and configurations for supported services, network objects, hosts, databases, Kubernetes platforms, and virtual machines.\n\n\n\n\n\n  How is data stored? \n\nThe results data that is generated by the service is stored in a Cloud Object Storage bucket that is owned by the customer. For help configuring storage, see [Storing data in Security and Compliance Center](https://cloud.ibm.com/docs/security-compliance?topic=security-compliance-storage).\n\n\n\n\n\n  Deleting your data",
